# What `teploy deploy` skips when syncing this directory to the server
# for the remote image build. The Dockerfile's builder stage compiles
# dist/ and web/dist/ ON the server, from the source synced here —
# src/, web/src/ (+ web config files), lockfiles, patches/ and deploy/
# runtime manifests are what the build needs.
#
# 2026-10-18, the incident that changed this file: the Dockerfile used to
# COPY a locally pre-built dist/ and web/dist/, and the sync shipped only
# those (source was excluded below), so nothing tied the image's code to
# the revision it was labelled with. Four deploys in a row shipped hours-
# old code. Source now travels instead of build output; dist/ never does.
#
# teploy-cli L14 (2026-09-24): the sync also honors .gitignore and never
# sends teploy config, overlays or env files. Build outputs (dist/,
# web/dist/, node_modules/) are gitignored and stay home; the builder
# stage in the Dockerfile re-creates them from this source.
.git
node_modules
reference
evals
swebench
_internal
# install.sh's secret bundle. It holds REAL values; the server already has
# them, age-encrypted, and a plaintext copy has no business riding along in a
# build context.
ship-secrets.env
*.secrets.env
